    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_88fe816cff9ece93f42e101ffcb4611ed6d4ed3b2200ddbd83bd7b5c94d9f4e4",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Planar nonzero-curvature L6 decoupling turns geometric separation at the N^(-1/2) parameter scale into an l2 assembly rule for local L6 pieces, and the discrete version carries the same control to coefficient-weighted exponential sums. Translation invariance makes that control reusable on localized balls. The gain is a precise lower-dimensional analytic interface; nonvanishing curvature and the prescribed scale remain essential, and this span does not establish any higher-dimensional factorization.",
