    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3178023568be6a5b464bdf2ac8830de6fd6ebc0a31d19614eef0329e5fc7e50e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Corollary 3 enters the exponential-sum argument through an exact interface: Fourier localization identifies the double-large-sieve first-spacing count A with A6(H; delta, H*delta), so the mean-value estimate bounds A. The large sieve then pairs that bound with independently supplied second-spacing estimates; choices of N and the refined window V balance the resulting terms and admissibility constraints, producing the short-sum exponent on its stated range. Complementary range estimates and the logarithmic-phase approximate functional equation then carry the bound to the critical-line zeta estimate.",
